h Barty"] " and the local favourite " [:a {:href "/athletes/144470"} "Naomi Osaka"] ", who had the honour of lighting the Olympic Flame at the 2020 opening ceremony."] "\n\n" [:p {} "America’s 11th seed " [:a {:href "/athletes/147286"} "Jennifer Brady"] " was eliminated in the first round, but the shock of the opening round was the defeat of top seed Barty by Spain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/142455"} "Sara Sorribes"] ", ranked 48th in the world. Osaka followed Barty out of the competition two rounds later when beaten by the unseeded " [:a {:href "/athletes/2101587"} "Markéta Vondroušová"] ". The highest ranked player left in the semi-finals was Ukraine’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/131994"} "Elina Svitolina"] " (No.4), but she was beaten by Vondroušová and, in the other semi, Switzerland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/146650"} "Belinda Bencic"] " beat " [:a {:href "/athletes/144760"} "Yelena Rybakina"] " of Kazakhstan."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the bronze medal match, fourth seed Elina Svitolina beat Rybakina, and won Ukraine’s first ever Olympic tennis medal. At one stage Svitolina was a set down and 1-3 down in the second set before staging a comeback. In the third and final set, Svitolina was 1-4 down, before winning the next five games in a row to win 6-4. On her Games début at the age of 24, Belinda Bencic beat Markéta Vondroušová in three sets to become the first Swiss woman to win an Olympic tennis gold."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/146650"} "Belinda Bencic"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/2101587"} "Markéta